  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale  \nThe problem is tackled using a hybrid algorithm combining genetic algorithms (GA) for global exploration and the SLSQP optimizer for local refinement. This approach leverages GA's ability to explore diverse solutions and SLSQP's precision in local optimization. The algorithm initialises from `initial_h_values` and systematically evolves candidate solutions, ensuring feasibility through constrained mutation and crossover operations. This method aims to escape local minima and discover\u66f4\u6709\u7ade\u4e89\u529b\u7684\u89e3\u3002\n\n2. Mathematical specification  \nVariables:  \n- h \u2208 \u211d^{n_points}, 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1, sum(h) = n_points / 2  \n- Fitness: max_k [convolve(h, 1 - h, mode='full')] * dx  \n\nObjective: Minimize fitness (C\u2085).  \nConstraints:  \n1. 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i  \n2. sum(h) = n_points / 2  \n\nImplementation steps:  \na. Population-based genetic search initialized from `initial_h_values`  \nb. Crossover combining segments from two parents  \nc. Mutation with constraint maintenance  \nd. Local SLSQP refinement of top candidates  \n\n3. Implementation procedure  \na. Initialization  \n   - Load `initial_h_values` (n=70)  \n   - Create initial population of 30 candidates by adding small perturbations to `initial_h_values`  \nb. GA loop  \n   - Evaluate C\u2085 for all candidates  \n   - Select top 50% based on C\u2085  \n   - Perform crossover on selected parents to generate new offspring  \n   - Apply mutation to offspring  \n   - Enforce constraints by clipping and normalizing  \n   - Apply SLSQP to top 10% candidates  \n   - Replace worst candidates with refined solutions  \nc. Termination after 600s or achieving C\u2085 \u2264 0.3807  \n\n4. Search choices  \n- Population size: 30  \n- Mutation rate: 0.05 (per element)  \n- Crossover rate: 0.7  \n- SLSQP iterations: 100 per candidate  \n- Elitism: Keep top 10%  \n\n5. Compute budget  \n- Population evaluation: ~50s per generation  \n- Expected 10-15 generations within 600s  \n\n6. Validation  \n- Ensure 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 and sum(h) = n_points / 2  \n- Re-check C\u2085 using evaluator  \n- Return best candidate meeting all constraints",
